Define class Fenwick:
```
class Fenwick:
    __slots__=("n","tree")
    def __init__(self,n): self.n=n; self.tree=[0]*(n+1)
    def add(self,i,delta=1):
        i+=1
        while i<=self.n: self.tree[i]+=delta; i+=i&-i
    def sum(self,i): # count in [0,i) if i is count? Maybe define prefix count first i positions.
        s=0
        while i>0: s+=self.tree[i]; i-=i&-i
        return s
```
